# Push to GitHub After Corrections

After you make any file edits, corrections, or fixes in this project:

1. **Stage** all changed files: `git add -A` (or stage only the files you modified).
2. **Commit** with a short, descriptive message (e.g. "Fix blog grid container; grid-only classes" or "Update X").
3. **Push** to GitHub: `git push origin main`.

Do this automatically in the same session—do not leave changes uncommitted or unpushed unless the user explicitly asks to skip it.

Use PowerShell-compatible command chaining: separate commands with `;` not `&&` (e.g. `git add -A; git commit -m "message"; git push origin main`).
